  "body": "## Why\n\nPR #1342 supplied rule/one-bar/snapshot contracts but no real producer-to-stateful-execution caller. The final user packet explicitly requests backend implementation, tests, integration, normal review/CI/PR/merge for the original 25 IDs and supersedes the BBIII same-day ban and Anti range-fade conflation. This is within the explicit exception in AGENTS.md; canonical frontend pre/post validation passed.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Implement five source groups covering the original 25 IDs, with source-direct rules, preserved frozen formula reuse and declared mechanical hypotheses separated.\n- Add a small versioned order/fill/ledger/snapshot adapter and bounded fixture dispatcher; preserve the existing execution_v2/metrics_v2/campaign_v2 and all frozen strategy/economic artifacts.\n- Prove one actual BBIII raw-fixture → confirmation → explicit fixture completion → modeled fills → account valuation path. Alpha dispatch needs no fabricated OHLC.\n- Bind full config, actual source/callable/dependency hashes, versions and input fingerprints. Reject gaps, invalid clocks, direction/symbol/quantity mismatches and uncertain intraminute order. Fix finite Decimal-to-float overflow.\n- Preserve the final packet text and all recovered prior evidence; publish per-25 remaining gaps, independent review corrections and a 80-file saved seal. Source Markdown hard-break spaces remain byte-for-byte as supplied.\n- Add saved-only CI; no data download, signal probe, FULL replay, service change, deployment, order, LIVE or promotion.\n\n## Actual validation\n\n- 1,344 Scalp7 synthetic/regression tests PASS (1,001 prior + 343 new).\n- Normal isolated Black/Ruff/Mypy/source-protection hooks and canonical frontend validation PASS.\n- All seven previous saved-publication checks PASS; new 80-file/25-row verifier PASS.\n- Independent execution, source, capital, pipeline and saved-verification reviews recorded under audits/.\n\n## Economic boundary and remaining work\n\n**New FULL 0; new real-history probes 0; new T/WR/Net/DD/winner damage unmeasured.** PR #1341 used 4/4 and the new scope has no allocation; no old budget is borrowed.\n\n25 dispatcher entries are not 25 complete source strategies. Only one raw-price fixture has end-to-end proof. Complete frozen economic baselines remain 0, with per-row source/mode/data/lifecycle closures still required. The current empty ready set needs 0 runs; future minimum and cap are undecided, not implicitly 25/50. Existing failures and grades remain unchanged. This PR completes an implementation increment, **not G4 economic development**.\n\nReports: research/campaigns/scalp7_20260920/implementation_v1/{FINAL_REPORT.md,COVERAGE.md,EXACT25_IMPLEMENTATION.json,VALIDATION.json,WORK_NEXT.txt}\n\nScope: G4_EXACT25_SOURCE_TO_CODE_IMPLEMENTATION_AFTER_FINAL_REVIEW_V1\nRefs #1334. No deployment required. Rollback is a normal code revert of this increment; retain previous research publications.\n\n## Review correction\n\nAt `b76beef250a345ca1464e19e5f5244e00978f3de`, both automated P2 findings were repaired: stale observed fills require detail replay, and only orders with cancellable pending/partial quantity can cancel. A related exact-boundary case excludes pre-entry detail from stops/MFE while preserving modeled intraminute ambiguity. Nine added regressions passed independently; full suite 1,344 PASS and refreshed 80-file seal PASS. Initial head and seal remain in git history; see audits/PR1343_REVIEW_FIXES.json.",
